        {
          "name": "Requested Samples",
          "type": "TArrayView<FVector3d>",
          "default": "TArrayView<const FVector3d>()"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Find negative space that should be protected. Uses the mesh passed on construction or to InitializeFromMesh or InitializeFromIndexMesh\n@param Settings\tSettings to use to find the negative space\n@return\t\t\tFalse on failure -- e.g., if there was no mesh available"
    },
    {
      "id": "compute",
      "name": "Compute",
      "category": "ConvexDecomposition3",
      "signature": "Compute(Target, Num Output Hulls, Num Additional Splits, Error Tolerance, Min Thickness Tolerance, Max Output Hulls, Only Split If Negative Space Covered)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FConvexDecomposition3*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Num Output Hulls",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "Num Additional Splits",
          "type": "Int",
          "default": "10"
        },
        {
          "name": "Error Tolerance",
          "type": "Double",
          "default": "0.0"
        },
        {
          "name": "Min Thickness Tolerance",
          "type": "Double",
          "default": "0"
        },
        {
          "name": "Max Output Hulls",
          "type": "Int",
          "default": "-1"
        },
        {
          "name": "Only Split If Negative Space Covered",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "false"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Compute a decomposition with the desired number of hulls\nNote: A future version of this function may replace NumOutputHulls with MaxOutputHulls, but this version keeps both parameters for compatibility / consistent behavior.\n@param NumOutputHulls\t\tNumber of convex hulls to use in the final convex decomposition\n@param NumAdditionalSplits\tHow far to go beyond the target number of hulls when initially the mesh into pieces -- larger values will require more computation but can find better convex decompositions\n@param ErrorTolerance\t\tStop splitting when hulls have error less than this (expressed in cm; will be cubed for volumetric error). Overrides NumOutputHulls if specified\n@param MinThicknessTolerance\tOptionally specify a minimum thickness (in cm) for convex parts; parts below this thickness will always be merged away. Overrides NumOutputHulls and ErrorTolerance when needed\n@param MaxOutputHulls\t\tIf > 0, maximum number of convex hulls to generate. Overrides ErrorTolerance and TargetNumParts when needed\n@param bOnlySplitIfOverlapNegativeSpace\tIf true, use NegativeSpace to guide splits, and only split parts that overlap negative space"
    },
    {
